WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.954
Ronald McDonald.

00:00:01.002 --> 00:00:04.234
He's a beloved character of American culture, an icon of culinary achievement,

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:07.722
and a symbol of fun, community, and childhood nostalgia.

00:00:07.786 --> 00:00:11.338
For generations, Ronald is a reminder of fun trips to McDonald's,

00:00:11.354 --> 00:00:13.834
chowing down on happy meals, exploring colorful play places,

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:16.430
and celebrating the values of friendship with a smile.

00:00:16.611 --> 00:00:24.000
♪ Put a smile on, put a smile on, everybody come on… put a smile on… ♪

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:29.010
Or... is he? Why is it that this supposed bastion of fun and happiness,

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:33.634
according to the McDonald's corporation, is perceived as creepy and unsettling by the general public? 

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:35.574
What other supposedly kid friendly fast

00:00:35.612 --> 00:00:39.654
food mascot finds himself tied over and over to nightmarish urban legends,

00:00:39.702 --> 00:00:42.502
disgusting controversies, and bizarre impersonations?

00:00:42.502 --> 00:00:43.818
Why is it that if you

00:00:43.824 --> 00:00:47.523
simply Google Ronald McDonald, half the results look like this?

00:00:47.523 --> 00:00:49.841
And this? And this?

00:00:49.841 --> 00:00:52.874
Why is the official company image of this character so vastly

00:00:52.922 --> 00:00:55.440
different from the discourse surrounding him?

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:03.840
-[Brittney] The Ronald McDonald statue looked down at this guy and said,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.203
-[Ronald] I'm tired too.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:13.200
-[Jessii] Ronald McDonald lurks in the ball pits, waiting to grab onto your leg,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.660
(Screams)

00:01:16.098 --> 00:01:17.751
-[Off Camera] That is so creepy… dude!

00:01:17.751 --> 00:01:23.732
♪ Ronald’s smile is just the thing that makes everybody sing! ♪

00:01:23.732 --> 00:01:26.365
–[Freaky] He gazed up at me with this disturbing smile…

00:01:26.365 --> 00:01:28.234
-[Ronald] Uh oh, there’s trouble afloat Billy.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.757
-[Reporter] ...and made Ronald a clown in hiding.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.401
-[Luke] Alright guys, they brought back Ronald McDonald.

00:01:32.401 --> 00:01:37.514
-[Reporter] McKayla can barely contain herself after hearing Ronald McDonald is back.

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:39.034
(Ronald laughing)

00:01:39.034 --> 00:01:41.643
-[Commercial] Ronald McDonald is now delivering smiles online!

00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:43.067
(Foreign threats)

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.080
-[Reporter] Watch. This

00:01:45.103 --> 00:01:46.599
(Screams)

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:49.322
-[Jamie] This is not fit for human consumption.

00:01:49.386 --> 00:01:50.634
-[Reporter] Family sued McDonald's.

00:01:50.682 --> 00:01:52.826
-[Reporter] McDonald's is a target of a major lawsuit.

00:01:52.858 --> 00:01:55.620
-[Akeem] McDonald's is being sued for almost a billion dollars.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:01.442
-[Reporter] The officers say with its red hair and a golden colored outfit,

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:02.930
-[Reporter] they knew exactly who this was.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.734
-[Reporter] It left a young girl disfigured.

00:02:04.782 --> 00:02:08.770
-[Reporter] Ronald McDonald's brand identity is one of happiness and welcoming, inviting

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.038
personality for children.

00:02:10.124 --> 00:02:13.526
-[Reporter] And I can't tell you how many parents will call and inquire because their

00:02:13.548 --> 00:02:14.920
-[Reporter] kids are freaking out.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.930
-[Akeem] Ba da ba ba ba. 

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.270
-[Akeem] They're not loving it.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.214
-[Nissim] We are slaves.

00:02:18.262 --> 00:02:21.130
-[Nissim] We have new God instead of the old God.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.930
-[Nissim] And we pray for McDonald's.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.930
(Screams)

00:02:26.209 --> 00:02:31.546
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.942
Welcome to Horror History.

00:02:34.096 --> 00:02:35.262
-[Ronald] Good morning, class.

00:02:35.396 --> 00:02:36.690
-[Hamburgers] Good morning, Ronald.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.518
Earlier this year, I made a Horror History episode on Grimace,

00:02:39.524 --> 00:02:42.526
The frightening, shake obsessed purple blob of nightmare fuel who came back in

00:02:42.548 --> 00:02:44.730
2023 to terrorize a new generation.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.678
In making that video, I ended up rediscovering a lot of disturbing

00:02:47.694 --> 00:02:50.270
information about the ringleader himself, Ronald McDonald.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:54.066
Ronald was first introduced as a new McDonald's mascot in 1963, taking over

00:02:54.088 --> 00:02:57.554
duties from the original mascot, Speedee, a perpetually winking or maybe

00:02:57.592 --> 00:03:01.106
Cyclops chef with a burger for a head and a penchant for productivity, named

00:03:01.138 --> 00:03:04.674
after the Speedee service system that cofounders Maurice and Richard McDonald

00:03:04.722 --> 00:03:06.082
used for their original restaurant.

00:03:06.146 --> 00:03:09.110
But according to Mashed.com, Speedee was dropped due to market research

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.858
showing that the Golden Arches themselves were a more iconic marketing symbol.

00:03:11.874 --> 00:03:15.386
So when it came time to produce TV commercials in the 1960s,

00:03:15.408 --> 00:03:16.534
a new mascot was developed.

00:03:16.582 --> 00:03:19.786
The original Ronald was a spiritual successor to Bozo the Clown with a

00:03:19.808 --> 00:03:23.098
Red and yellow striped jumpsuit, a shake cup for a nose, a cardboard tray as a

00:03:23.104 --> 00:03:26.078
hat and a crazed look in his eye, giving him more of an appearance of an

00:03:26.084 --> 00:03:27.914
unhinged hobo than a circus performer.

00:03:27.962 --> 00:03:30.366
Ronald's appearance would change over the years with the intention of

00:03:30.388 --> 00:03:31.438
appealing more to children.

00:03:31.524 --> 00:03:34.766
And while it is normal for any corporate mascot to be created with the

00:03:34.788 --> 00:03:37.934
intention of advertising to the youth, Ronald's targeting of prepubescence

00:03:37.982 --> 00:03:41.666
gets much darker than any of the competition, except for maybe Jared from Subway.

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.806
That guy was kind of !@#$%.

00:03:43.838 --> 00:03:46.898
Surprisingly, if we look closely at the official McDonald's messaging, we can see proof of

00:03:46.904 --> 00:03:50.102
occult activities being performed by Ronald right out in open air.

00:03:50.156 --> 00:03:53.494
But to understand how a children's character became so synonymous with horror,

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:56.630
we've got to take it all the way back to his birth.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.630
(IMPACT)

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.930
Willard Scott was born on March 7, 1934.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.886
From a young age, he took an interest in broadcasting and formed a

00:04:06.918 --> 00:04:08.630
Radio club in his neighborhood with other boys.

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:12.486
After some success in radio, he moved on to television in the 1950s, mostly

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:16.282
appearing in children's shows like Barn Party, Afternoon, Commander Retro,

00:04:16.346 --> 00:04:17.658
and Bozo the Clown.

00:04:17.754 --> 00:04:21.086
Even then, he wanted to gain influence over kids, but we wouldn't find out

00:04:21.108 --> 00:04:22.270
why for some time.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.566
Originally created as a mascot for Capitol Records, Bozo was spun off into

00:04:25.588 --> 00:04:28.354
his own franchise, with different actors playing him in different local

00:04:28.392 --> 00:04:29.326
radio stations.

00:04:29.438 --> 00:04:34.942
Scott played Bozo on WRCTV from 1959 to 1962, when the show was canceled.

00:04:35.006 --> 00:04:38.354
A year later, one of the show's sponsors, McDonald's, approached Scott about

00:04:38.392 --> 00:04:41.046
helping them develop a character for three local commercial spots in

00:04:41.068 --> 00:04:41.686
Washington, DC.

00:04:41.708 --> 00:04:44.002
And the result was Ronald McDonald.

00:04:44.066 --> 00:04:46.994
He mostly looked the same as Bozo, borrowing the bright red smile, curved

00:04:47.042 --> 00:04:48.754
eyebrows, and exaggerated collar.

00:04:48.802 --> 00:04:51.750
But what Willard Scott created was more than just a new character.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.866
It was a new identity, a change akin to Norma Jean Baker saying goodbye to

00:04:55.888 --> 00:04:59.414
her old life to become Marilyn Monroe, Stefani Germanotta’s transformation into

00:04:59.462 --> 00:05:03.462
Lady Gaga, or Shane Lee Yaw's rebranding to become Shane Dawson.

00:05:03.526 --> 00:05:07.118
You could say that Ronald McDonald was truly born that day, but for the

00:05:07.124 --> 00:05:10.158
purposes of making my thumbnail look more impressive, I will not.

00:05:10.244 --> 00:05:13.006
Also, there's this one commercial where Ronald reminisces about his

00:05:13.028 --> 00:05:16.170
childhood and losing his first tooth, where he was still a clown.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.866
But I think it's safe to say that this is a fictionalized version of the events.

00:05:18.888 --> 00:05:22.206
But don't tell that to the McDonald's corporation, who still insist

00:05:22.238 --> 00:05:26.630
that Ronald McDonald is a real person, making no mention of any actors.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:34.310
-[Commercial] Introducing the world's newest, silliest and hamburger eatingest clown,

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.550
-[Commercial] Ronald McDonald.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:42.054
-[Commercial] Now, where is that clown? Oh, Ronald, Ronald, Ronald.

00:05:42.182 --> 00:05:43.126
-[Commercial] Hey, Ronald.

00:05:43.238 --> 00:05:44.218
-[Ronald] Here I am, kid.

00:05:44.304 --> 00:05:47.162
Yep, the world's first introduction to Ronald would be in a dark room,

00:05:47.216 --> 00:05:51.110
crouched over an analog TV, addressing a group of children... in secret.

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:53.706
Knowing that it's kind of shocking that nobody figured out this guy would

00:05:53.728 --> 00:05:54.982
become a thing of nightmares.

00:05:55.046 --> 00:05:58.362
He was so in touch with his scary side that in just his second commercial,

00:05:58.426 --> 00:06:01.422
he ended up inspiring one of the greatest horror icons of all time,

00:06:01.476 --> 00:06:03.466
Pennywise from Stephen King's IT.

00:06:03.588 --> 00:06:06.622
-[Ronald] Waha. Isn't that McDonald's hamburger? Delicious.

00:06:06.686 --> 00:06:09.246
-[Kid] Mom told me never to talk to strangers.

00:06:09.358 --> 00:06:10.930
-[Pennywise] Hi Georgie. Don't you want a balloon?

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:16.818
-[Georgie] I'm not supposed to take stuff to the stranger.

00:06:16.994 --> 00:06:18.598
-[Georgie] My dad said so.

00:06:18.764 --> 00:06:20.502
-[Ronald] Well, your mother's right, as always.

00:06:20.556 --> 00:06:22.242
-[Ronald] But I'm Ronald McDonald.

00:06:22.306 --> 00:06:23.650
-[Ronald] Give me a McDonald's shake.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.082
-[Pennywise] Very wise of your dad, Georgie.

00:06:26.146 --> 00:06:27.670
-[Pennywise] Very wise indeed.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:32.810
-[Pennywise] I, Georgie, am Pennywise, the dancing clown.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.850
-[Pennywise] You are Georgie.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.994
-[Pennywise] So now we know each other.

00:06:38.112 --> 00:06:41.706
But these seemingly predatory lines are not the only similarity that Ronald

00:06:41.738 --> 00:06:42.714
shares with Pennywise.

00:06:42.762 --> 00:06:46.350
And these initial commercials all contain a clue to understanding his true

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.390
motivation.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:50.023
(IMAPCT)

