00:08:00.211 --> 00:08:03.930
♪ Suspenseful Music ♪

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:06.274
In the initial round of Ronald McDonald's commercials,

00:08:06.322 --> 00:08:09.622
There's one often overlooked odity that puts Ronald on a different level

00:08:09.676 --> 00:08:10.642
than Bozo the Clown.

00:08:10.706 --> 00:08:14.314
Ronald has the ability to wield magic, and he even says as much in his first commercial.

00:08:14.352 --> 00:08:17.062
-[Ronald] A magic tray here keeps me well supplied.

00:08:17.126 --> 00:08:19.990
-[Ronald] McDonald's hamburgers, french fries, and milkshakes.

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:23.262
In his second ad, he uses the tray to gain the trust of a child.

00:08:23.396 --> 00:08:25.658
-[Kid] Well, you sound like Ronald.

00:08:25.754 --> 00:08:26.814
-[Ronald] Here, I'll prove it.

00:08:26.852 --> 00:08:28.830
-[Ronald] I'll give you three more hamburgers.

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:34.298
-[Ronald] I know you’re not supposed to accept gifts from strangers either.

00:08:34.314 --> 00:08:35.050
-[Kid] But you’re no stranger,

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:37.242
-[Kid] You really are Ronald McDonald.

00:08:37.306 --> 00:08:40.274
In an interview with the Food Network, Ronald eventually admitted his true

00:08:40.312 --> 00:08:42.590
goal with these commercials and the design of his character.

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:46.755
There was something about the combination of hamburgers and Bozo that was irresistible to kids.

00:08:47.098 --> 00:08:50.776
-[Commercial] Ronald McDonald the world famous magical clown.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:54.646
Can we think of anyone else who used magic to take the form of a clown to

00:08:54.668 --> 00:08:58.294
lure in children? It reminds me a lot of this passage from Chapter 21 in IT.

00:08:58.332 --> 00:09:01.762
The fears of children were simpler and usually more powerful.

00:09:01.826 --> 00:09:04.682
The fears of children could often be summoned up in a single face.

00:09:04.736 --> 00:09:08.598
And if bait were needed, why? What child did not love a clown?

00:09:08.614 --> 00:09:11.818
That brings me to the third Ronald McDonald's commercial, in which Ronald grabs onto a

00:09:11.824 --> 00:09:14.954
rocket and flies to the moon, where there is already a McDonald's restaurant. 

00:09:15.002 --> 00:09:17.742
Clearly, more magic was employed to make this happen.

00:09:17.796 --> 00:09:20.746
And clearly this is another parallel shared with Pennywise, the dancing clown

00:09:20.778 --> 00:09:23.866
Who initially came to Earth as a crash landing meteor from outer space.

00:09:23.898 --> 00:09:27.538
As I mentioned, in our world, Pennywise is nothing more than a

00:09:27.544 --> 00:09:30.334
fictional character that was inspired partially by Ronald McDonald.

00:09:30.382 --> 00:09:33.922
But perhaps Stephen King came to realize the true horror of Ronald's power

00:09:33.976 --> 00:09:36.162
and fictionalized it as a warning to all of us.

00:09:36.216 --> 00:09:40.034
Ronald is brought up no less than three times in King's novel, most notably

00:09:40.082 --> 00:09:43.586
by Don Haggerty, who, after witnessing Pennywise kill his boyfriend,

00:09:43.618 --> 00:09:46.690
claimed that the clown looked like a cross between Ronald McDonald and Bozo.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.858
Ronald's plan seemed to be working because after these initial commercials,

00:09:49.874 --> 00:09:53.258
which aired around Washington, DC, he became a local celebrity and gained a

00:09:53.264 --> 00:09:55.590
lot of influence over children near the nation's capital.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:58.698
This led to him being introduced nationally in 1966.

00:09:58.784 --> 00:10:01.674
Before appearing on the national stage, Ronald got his first of many

00:10:01.712 --> 00:10:04.926
makeovers, dropping the drink-cup nose and tray hat and adopting a more

00:10:04.948 --> 00:10:06.074
traditional clown costume.

00:10:06.122 --> 00:10:09.386
Is it coincidence that this look would seemingly go on to inspire serial

00:10:09.418 --> 00:10:12.606
killer John Wayne Gacy? Or was that simply the standard clown look at the time?

00:10:12.628 --> 00:10:14.010
I'll let you decide.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.990
In what some sources have documented as the first national commercial,

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:20.466
Ronald helps paint a McDonald's sign sticks around for lunch, then takes off

00:10:20.488 --> 00:10:23.666
in his flying hamburger mobile, obviously another demonstration of his

00:10:23.688 --> 00:10:24.418
occult power.

00:10:24.504 --> 00:10:27.598
Another commercial once again shows him using magic to conjure McDonald's

00:10:27.614 --> 00:10:29.994
menu items to fuel his flying burger mobile.

00:10:30.062 --> 00:10:32.726
I love how this early commercial really takes the time to demonstrate how

00:10:32.748 --> 00:10:36.162
Ronald can easily become a source of fear when his vehicle backfires.

00:10:36.226 --> 00:10:37.750
Just listen to their screams.

00:10:37.963 --> 00:10:42.378
(explosion) (children screams)
–[Ronald] Looks like I’m having trouble getting started.

00:10:42.464 --> 00:10:45.226
Over the next couple years, he gained a lot of recognition starring in

00:10:45.248 --> 00:10:48.614
commercials during the Macy's Thanksgiving Day parade and NFL championship game.

00:10:48.662 --> 00:10:51.542
But most of the ads played on children's programming.

00:10:51.606 --> 00:10:55.226
Why was there such a great focus on targeting kids? In one particularly

00:10:55.258 --> 00:10:59.114
creepy commercial from the 1960s, he possibly reveals the true motivation

00:10:59.162 --> 00:11:02.640
when he's unloading food from a carryout bag and discovers a child inside.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:08.658
–[Ronald] Say, you sure can get a lot in these bags, can’t you?

00:11:08.664 --> 00:11:11.426
It's never made clear if Ronald was planning on eating that child, but photos from the time

00:11:11.448 --> 00:11:14.946
Do demonstrate a chilling contrast between a very elated looking Ronald

00:11:14.968 --> 00:11:16.642
and a very uncomfortable looking child.

00:11:16.776 --> 00:11:19.762
With the success of these initial commercials, the McDonald's corporation

00:11:19.826 --> 00:11:21.750
went all in on advertising to kids.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:25.426
In 1970, they put Ronald in a series of comics sold on newsstands.

00:11:25.458 --> 00:11:28.594
And the following year, Ronald was promoted to Chief Happiness Officer,

00:11:28.642 --> 00:11:31.786
which came with a relocation into McDonald Land, home to many other

00:11:31.808 --> 00:11:35.414
McDonald's characters like Officer Big Mac, Mayor McCheese, The Professor,

00:11:35.462 --> 00:11:39.622
the Hamburglar, Captain Crook, the Goblins, AND The Evil Grimace.

00:11:39.766 --> 00:11:42.954
McDonald Land is basically a preserve where fast food items can be found

00:11:42.992 --> 00:11:43.702
growing in nature.

00:11:43.766 --> 00:11:46.814
But it's also kind of weird that most of the inhabitants, like Officer Big Mac

00:11:46.852 --> 00:11:49.550
and Mayor McCheese, are fast food items themselves.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:52.874
Pretty much every character plays into this theme of law versus crime.

00:11:52.922 --> 00:11:56.506
But why is the law enforcing a culture that encourages human kids feasting

00:11:56.538 --> 00:11:59.442
down on their own people? Is Mayor McCheees not worried about these kids

00:11:59.496 --> 00:12:02.882
developing a taste for his own flesh by eating at McDonald's?

00:12:02.936 --> 00:12:06.658
The only reasonable explanation is that Ronald, with his new CHO position

00:12:06.664 --> 00:12:09.090
at the McDonald's corporation, is the one pulling the strings here.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:12.406
He's trying to fatten these kids up for something, perhaps some kind of ritual.

00:12:12.428 --> 00:12:15.906
Most of the commercials feature Ronald doing something to outsmart

00:12:15.938 --> 00:12:19.030
and stop one of the villainous characters from stealing McDonald's food,

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:23.078
which, again, is readily available to be picked and eaten in nature.

00:12:23.174 --> 00:12:26.314
One of these commercials features Ronald pulling items out of a magic top hat.

00:12:26.352 --> 00:12:29.942
It's not outside the typical scope of work for clowns to perform magic,

00:12:30.006 --> 00:12:33.206
but what is striking is that this is basically the only kind of performance

00:12:33.238 --> 00:12:33.732
that he does up to this point.

00:12:33.732 --> 00:12:37.546
We haven't seen him juggling, riding a unicycle, miming,

00:12:37.578 --> 00:12:41.018
or doing any other activities typically associated with being a clown.

00:12:41.114 --> 00:12:44.686
Ronald could easily have chosen to make himself a hamburger magician,

00:12:44.708 --> 00:12:45.706
but he didn't do that.

00:12:45.828 --> 00:12:48.098
Why? Because he wants to appeal to kids.

00:12:48.184 --> 00:12:51.282
He's constantly saying things to make himself seem more relatable to kids,

00:12:51.336 --> 00:12:54.050
who he constantly refers to as the boys and girl.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:57.906
-[Ronald] Now McDonald's everywhere will have plenty of scrumptious cherry pies for

00:12:57.928 --> 00:12:59.958
-[Ronald] boys and girls to enjoy any time.

00:13:00.044 --> 00:13:03.366
Since Pennywise seems to be modeled after Ronald, it's probably safe to use

00:13:03.388 --> 00:13:04.290
IT as a reference.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:07.138
Its power literally comes from consuming the kid's fear.

00:13:07.234 --> 00:13:13.910
-[Pennywise] Take all of you and I'll feast on your flesh as I feed on your fear.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:17.226
There's not enough evidence so far to say that Ronald is eating the children,

00:13:17.248 --> 00:13:20.870
but I do think they're connected to his ability to harness magic,

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:23.530
which, by the way, is getting more and more unsettling.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:27.178
Take this commercial from the 1970s, where a boy named Aaron first discovers

00:13:27.194 --> 00:13:28.554
the McDonald's PlayLand.

00:13:28.682 --> 00:13:31.294
-[Ronald] Welcome, Eric, to McDonaldland.

00:13:31.412 --> 00:13:34.718
Yep, the statue has begun talking.

00:13:34.884 --> 00:13:35.874
Oh, my God.

00:13:35.992 --> 00:13:40.274
Why the close ups? What is happening?

00:13:40.312 --> 00:13:41.426
-[Ronald] Of course it's me and all your other friends, too.

00:13:41.608 --> 00:13:43.554
-[Ronald] Come on in and look around.

00:13:43.672 --> 00:13:47.506
Why did that sound so threatening? I just want you to remember that in 70s,

00:13:47.528 --> 00:13:51.014
The statue talked in an official McDonald's production, just in case.

00:13:51.132 --> 00:13:52.342
Oh, I don't know.

00:13:52.396 --> 00:13:55.078
The company tries to deny something like this happening later on.

00:13:55.164 --> 00:13:58.114
This was actually a short film directed at prospective McDonald's

00:13:58.162 --> 00:14:01.410
franchisees to educate them on the newest option to increase business at

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.990
their stores, the installation of a McDonald's PlayLand.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:07.046
Ronald and the other characters had become so popular that their likenesses

00:14:07.078 --> 00:14:09.622
were being used in playground equipment at McDonald's restaurants.

00:14:09.686 --> 00:14:13.134
However, as we have seen with many popular characters over the years, with

00:14:13.172 --> 00:14:16.858
clout often comes controversy, and Ronald McDonald was about to be

00:14:16.858 --> 00:14:18.030
taken to court.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:20.030
(IMPACT)

00:14:23.127 --> 00:14:26.439
♪  Suspenseful Music ♪

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:30.834
Have you ever heard the term sued out of existence? Turns out it's not just hyperbole.

00:14:30.872 --> 00:14:34.194
That's exactly what the McDonald land characters were facing when

00:14:34.232 --> 00:14:37.026
Sid and Marty Krofft, the creators of the children's television show

00:14:37.048 --> 00:14:39.618
H.R. Pufnstuf, sued Ronald and the gang for their resemblance to the

00:14:39.624 --> 00:14:40.610
Pufnstuf characters starting in 1973.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:44.806
The main point of contention was Mayor McCheese, who was

00:14:44.828 --> 00:14:47.938
accused of infringing the copyright of Mayor H.R. Pufnstuf himself.

00:14:48.034 --> 00:14:51.098
It was a long and hard fought affair, but in the end, Pufnstuf and the

00:14:51.104 --> 00:14:54.438
Krofft brothers were victorious, which is especially surprising considering

00:14:54.454 --> 00:14:59.020
that Mayor McCheese himself is also the judge in McDonaldland.

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:01.020
-[Mayor McCheese] Order! Order in the court!

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:04.566
During the surely very expensive lawsuit, the characters are forced to sleep

00:15:04.598 --> 00:15:05.654
outside in beds.

00:15:05.702 --> 00:15:09.246
I don't know if McDonald's typically has a very rainy climate, but snow is

00:15:09.268 --> 00:15:10.478
certainly not out of the question.

00:15:10.564 --> 00:15:13.258
Perhaps to save face against the bad press generated by the legal proceedings,

00:15:13.274 --> 00:15:16.266
Ronald decided to start his own charity foundation,

00:15:16.298 --> 00:15:18.226
aptly titled the Ronald McDonald House.

00:15:18.328 --> 00:15:21.374
Kind of ironic considering that he was still living in a group of beds

00:15:21.422 --> 00:15:22.578
sitting in an open field.

00:15:22.664 --> 00:15:25.538
But Ronald McDonald's house provided shelter and support to families of

00:15:25.544 --> 00:15:27.698
children undergoing surgeries and medical care.

00:15:27.784 --> 00:15:30.886
It was a very successful program, but it would eventually be the center of

00:15:30.908 --> 00:15:32.210
some appalling horror stories.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:33.190
More on that later.

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:36.278
Also during the Krofft Brothers litigation, McDonald's produced a series of

00:15:36.284 --> 00:15:39.250
toys showcasing the characters of their McDonaldland commercial cast.

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:42.166
I talked about this in the Grimace video, but these are some pretty terror

00:15:42.198 --> 00:15:43.366
inducing figurines.

00:15:43.478 --> 00:15:46.538
As someone who has now been through the process of producing a figurine,

00:15:46.544 --> 00:15:49.190
I don't know how McDonald's and Remco messed up so badly.

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:52.534
These children's toys make your flesh creep, with one of the worst offenders

00:15:52.582 --> 00:15:55.326
being Huggy the Tree, whose appearance has already been described as

00:15:55.348 --> 00:15:57.290
uncomfortable and just upsetting.

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:00.686
But Ronald, the leader of the pack, was not to be outdone because they made

00:16:00.708 --> 00:16:02.734
the toy just have these pitch black eyes.

00:16:02.852 --> 00:16:06.106
It would be easy to chalk this up to poor toy design, but I think there's

00:16:06.138 --> 00:16:06.962
something more here.

00:16:07.016 --> 00:16:10.258
There are several other instances of Ronald's eyes going pitch black.

00:16:10.344 --> 00:16:13.758
It can even be seen on more modern official posts from the Ronald McDonald Instagram. 

00:16:13.774 --> 00:16:17.266
This may be something involuntary that happens to Ronald from

00:16:17.288 --> 00:16:20.274
time to time, like perhaps after the use of dark magic.

00:16:20.322 --> 00:16:23.078
And it just so happened to occur while he was being photographed for the action figure.

00:16:23.084 --> 00:16:26.534
Ronald's dabbling in the occult is starting to become more evident. 

00:16:26.572 --> 00:16:30.806
In 1977, Sid and Marty Krofft won the lawsuit against McDonald, and

00:16:30.828 --> 00:16:33.814
although there would be an appeal and another ten years of legal fighting,

00:16:33.862 --> 00:16:36.678
many characters were forced to retire in the 1980s as they were slowly

00:16:36.694 --> 00:16:40.214
phased out of McDonald land, including Mayor McCheese, Officer Big Mac,

00:16:40.262 --> 00:16:41.942
Captain Crook, and The Professor.

00:16:42.006 --> 00:16:43.690
Ronald luckily made the cut.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:46.634
He and the other remaining characters would continue to star in commercials

00:16:46.682 --> 00:16:50.126
like this one, where Ronald uses his magic pogo stick to meet the Man in the Moon.

00:16:50.148 --> 00:16:51.902
No, not that Moon Man,

00:16:51.956 --> 00:16:52.874
Internet users.

00:16:52.922 --> 00:16:54.842
Maybe we'll get to him in a different episode.

00:16:54.906 --> 00:16:59.026
He actually goes to the moon again and again and again and again.

00:16:59.128 --> 00:17:00.782
They love sending Ronald to the Moon.

00:17:00.846 --> 00:17:02.910
Maybe there really is some deeper connection.

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:06.018
He also starred in a commercial promoting the Flying McNuggets, where the

00:17:06.024 --> 00:17:08.386
clown is in an actual circus for once.

00:17:08.488 --> 00:17:12.034
He was also there in 1986 for the arrival of Birdie the Early Bird's egg.

00:17:12.082 --> 00:17:14.854
It seems that he and the gang are still sleeping outside, which really

00:17:14.892 --> 00:17:17.686
raises some questions about how much they actually make from all these

00:17:17.708 --> 00:17:18.434
commercial gigs.

00:17:18.482 --> 00:17:20.934
I was wondering earlier what they do during inclement weather.

00:17:20.982 --> 00:17:24.294
And that seems to be answered in this commercial, Midnight at McDonald's,

00:17:24.342 --> 00:17:27.770
where we find out he just sleeps on the floor in the kitchen at McDonald's.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:29.490
-[Hamburger] Psst! Ronald! Wake up.

00:17:30.253 --> 00:17:32.623
-[Ronald] Hey, we gotta get ready for the kids tomorrow!

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:36.254
Imagine being a fry cook who works at McDonald's and you forget something

00:17:36.292 --> 00:17:37.550
and have to go back at night.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:42.254
You fumble around in the dark and that's when you hear snoring coming from

00:17:42.292 --> 00:17:43.310
right below you.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:47.278
You slowly look down to find a man in full clown attire passed out on the floor.

00:17:47.284 --> 00:17:50.478
Sounds about as relaxing as being the night security at

00:17:50.494 --> 00:17:51.550
Freddie Fazbear's Pizza.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:54.418
The main difference with Ronald's appearances in the 80s is that many of

00:17:54.424 --> 00:17:57.090
them take place in our world rather than McDonaldland.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:18:00.626
He teaches a class of burgers, stars in musical numbers, dances with trash cans,

00:18:00.658 --> 00:18:04.278
travels through time, feeds a robot McDonald's food, for some reason,

00:18:04.364 --> 00:18:08.198
feeds an alien McDonald's food, produces a play, produces a movie,

00:18:08.204 --> 00:18:09.122
becomes a private investigator,

00:18:09.186 --> 00:18:12.646
Becomes a competitive cyclist, Becomes a newspaper publisher, joins a folk band,

00:18:12.678 --> 00:18:16.454
joins a rock band, joins a hip hop group, joins the military, plays piano,

00:18:16.502 --> 00:18:19.946
takes a sleigh ride, shows off his ice skating skills, plays some baseball,

00:18:19.968 --> 00:18:23.286
plays some basketball, lifts some weights,

00:18:23.318 --> 00:18:24.202
competes in several Olympic sports.

00:18:24.266 --> 00:18:27.566
Climbs a mountain, goes on a treasure hunt, goes to the library, goes to Transylvania,

00:18:27.588 --> 00:18:31.486
goes on a submarine voyage, goes to fairytale land, goes to the mushroom kingdom,

00:18:31.508 --> 00:18:34.798
creates a portal to a winter realm and puts the Chicken McNuggets to bed,

00:18:34.804 --> 00:18:37.666
which is kind of terrifying from their perspective. 

00:18:37.688 --> 00:18:41.394
And through everything, eats a really concerning amount of

00:18:41.432 --> 00:18:44.558
McDonald's food while somehow putting on no visible weight.

00:18:44.654 --> 00:18:47.346
Another difference is that Grimace and the Hamburglar are now friends with

00:18:47.368 --> 00:18:48.670
Ronald rather than enemies.

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:52.038
They take part in the kids product mania of the 1980s, with Ronald and

00:18:52.044 --> 00:18:55.046
Grimace appearing in a children's book and even an animated short film that

00:18:55.068 --> 00:18:57.394
played at birthday parties inside McDonald's restaurants.

00:18:57.442 --> 00:19:01.606
One of Ronald's greatest rivals, Charles Entertainment Cheese, was going

00:19:01.628 --> 00:19:04.810
through a rough patch at the time, one of many rough patches, actually.

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:07.946
So the clown decided to kick him while he's down and steal one of his main

00:19:07.968 --> 00:19:08.950
sources of income.

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:10.230
Birthday parties.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:14.874
-[Commercial] There's food, fun and games for the kids and even

00:19:14.922 --> 00:19:15.770
-[Commercial] a special McDonald's birthday cake.

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:19.598
-[Commercial] A McDonald's birthday party gives him something to remember all year long.

00:19:19.684 --> 00:19:22.606
Yes, because being surrounded by a huddle of friends wearing Grimace hats is

00:19:22.628 --> 00:19:24.218
exactly how I want to spend my birthday.

00:19:24.314 --> 00:19:27.214
Anyway, the short film that played for birthdays features Ronald and friends

00:19:27.252 --> 00:19:30.386
in a series of adventures across space and time in a vehicle called the

00:19:30.408 --> 00:19:32.786
Adventure Machine, which looks an awful lot like

00:19:32.808 --> 00:19:34.110
HG Wells time machine.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:37.410
You would think they'd be more careful about potential intellectual property

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:41.078
theft after literally just getting sued, but nothing would come out of this.

00:19:41.164 --> 00:19:44.326
But since this movie is animated, there's this part where Ronald's head is

00:19:44.348 --> 00:19:47.154
in the foreground, and at first I thought Grimace had just opened his mouth

00:19:47.202 --> 00:19:48.840
ridiculously wide open.

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:54.086
This short came out in 1987, but Ronald's biggest claim to Hollywood fame

00:19:54.118 --> 00:19:56.612
was yet to come the following year, when he would appear in a 

00:19:56.612 --> 00:19:58.410
major motion picture.

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:00.410
(IMPACT)

00:20:02.878 --> 00:20:04.878
♪  Creepy Clown Music ♪

00:20:04.878 --> 00:20:09.070
-[Ronald] Hi kids, it's me, Ronald McDonald, and I'm on the set of my very first

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:10.670
-[Ronald] motion picture ever.

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:15.280
-[Ronald] It's a movie called Mac and Me and I want to introduce you to him.

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:19.186
Mac and Me was a blatant ripoff of E.T.,

00:20:19.208 --> 00:20:22.094
The 1982 hit directed by Steven Spielberg.

00:20:22.142 --> 00:20:24.974
The movie featured a twelve year old triple boy who befriends an alien

00:20:25.022 --> 00:20:27.102
accidentally brought back to Earth by a NASA rover.

00:20:27.166 --> 00:20:30.386
The alien becomes known as Mac, presumably named after the Big Mac,

00:20:30.418 --> 00:20:32.310
McDonald's signature menu item.

00:20:32.428 --> 00:20:35.234
–[Eric] It’s the thing I’ve been telling you about, the MAC!

00:20:35.234 --> 00:20:37.459
–[Michael] What?
–[Eric] The Mysterious Alien Creature.

00:20:37.459 --> 00:20:42.598
According to Thrillist, the film's producer, R. J. Louis claims similarities to the Big Mac are a complete coincidence,

00:20:42.694 --> 00:20:45.770
which is very difficult to believe because of the relentless product

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:49.494
placement throughout the entire rest of the movie.

00:20:49.542 --> 00:20:52.678
-[Drew] Rather than a bad movie that's occasionally interrupted by some product placement.

00:20:52.774 --> 00:20:57.614
-[Drew] Mac and Me is an hour and a half long commercial

00:20:57.652 --> 00:20:58.152
-[Drew] occasionally interrupted by a movie.

00:20:58.186 --> 00:21:01.006
Though the people involved claim that the movie was not directly funded by McDonald's,

00:21:01.028 --> 00:21:04.078
it was part of a vision to sell movie products through the McDonald's brand,

00:21:04.084 --> 00:21:07.806
and it may have been funded by McDonald's supplier,

00:21:07.838 --> 00:21:08.542
Golden State Foods.

00:21:08.606 --> 00:21:12.082
ET's popularity had helped boost the sales of Reese's pieces six years earlier,

00:21:12.136 --> 00:21:15.666
so it seems that RJ Louis maybe believed that his movie

00:21:15.688 --> 00:21:16.120
could do the same.

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.982
Thrillist states that Louis had worked on McDonald's campaigns in the past

00:21:19.036 --> 00:21:21.538
and remained close with Ronald McDonald's house charities.

00:21:21.634 --> 00:21:25.574
In other words, Ronald himself was Louis's in to acquire the rights to use

00:21:25.612 --> 00:21:26.642
the McDonald's brand.

00:21:26.706 --> 00:21:29.750
From Ronald's perspective, there was no reason to help Louis with this,

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:33.010
except for the opportunity to be exposed to more kids.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:36.134
Ronald was already considered one of the most famous faces on the planet at this point.

00:21:36.182 --> 00:21:39.194
Some of the proceeds of the movie would also be donated to

00:21:39.232 --> 00:21:40.022
Ronald's charity.

00:21:40.086 --> 00:21:44.386
The film opened on August 12, 1988, and Ronald's appearance is a brief cameo

00:21:44.438 --> 00:21:46.298
during a birthday party at McDonald's.

00:21:46.394 --> 00:21:49.726
Despite the limited scope of his role, he still managed to win an award for

00:21:49.748 --> 00:21:50.490
his performance.

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:54.218
The award was the Golden Raspberry Award for Worst New Star, and the movie

00:21:54.234 --> 00:21:58.094
as a whole was very poorly received, grossing just $6 million on a

00:21:58.142 --> 00:22:00.594
13 million budget and being pulled after just two weeks.

00:22:00.712 --> 00:22:04.766
This utter humiliation seemed not to deter Ronald from continuing to branch

00:22:04.798 --> 00:22:05.954
out into other mediums.

00:22:06.002 --> 00:22:09.346
The following year, he starred in a Japanese Nintendo game called Donald Land,

00:22:09.378 --> 00:22:12.920
Which has creepy faces and horror elements written all over it.

00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:19.814
What the hell is that thing? Then, in the game, Ronald has to save his friends

00:22:19.852 --> 00:22:21.662
from a series of eldritch abominations.

00:22:21.746 --> 00:22:25.030
It's interesting that the final boss is also a magic wielding clown.

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:28.666
Is this ultimately what Ronald will become if he continues down this path of

00:22:28.688 --> 00:22:30.890
sorcery and witchcraft? Time would tell.

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:34.522
In the 1990s, his cult continued to grow with the 1990 direct to video

00:22:34.576 --> 00:22:37.402
release the Adventures of Ronald McDonald's McTreasure Island.

00:22:37.466 --> 00:22:41.230
In 1992, he almost seems to be openly inviting children to join the cult

00:22:41.300 --> 00:22:45.202
when he releases a new ad campaign called Do You Believe in Magic?

00:22:45.256 --> 00:22:49.991
♪ When you believe in magic? Only Ronald can do! ♪

00:22:50.150 --> 00:22:53.982
He also crossed into the US video game market with a video game adaptation

00:22:54.046 --> 00:22:57.490
called McDonald's Treasure Land Adventure for the Sega. Up to this point,

00:22:57.560 --> 00:23:01.142
despite a few eyebrow raising incidents, Ronald mostly had a very clean image.

00:23:01.196 --> 00:23:04.514
It's very easy for me to cherry pick moments where he seemed creepy,

00:23:04.562 --> 00:23:07.906
but over his first 30 years with the company, there are really only a

00:23:07.938 --> 00:23:08.770
handful of examples.

00:23:08.850 --> 00:23:12.826
He was an icon of pop culture with a devoted fanbase or perhaps cult of

00:23:12.848 --> 00:23:14.682
young children supporting his every move.

00:23:14.736 --> 00:23:18.778
But it's during the 1990s that rumors of sinister behavior start to rise to

00:23:18.784 --> 00:23:19.478
the surface.

00:23:19.574 --> 00:23:21.738
Literally. Let's rewind a couple of years.

00:23:21.824 --> 00:23:24.738
Remember how I said that Ronald wanted to kick his pizza snarfing rival

00:23:24.774 --> 00:23:28.254
Charles while he was down in the 1980s by offering birthday parties?

00:23:28.292 --> 00:23:30.126
That wasn't the only shot fired at Chuck E. Cheese's, 

00:23:30.148 --> 00:23:34.286
because in 1987 McDonald's introduced the McDonald's PlayPlace,

00:23:34.308 --> 00:23:38.514
A softer, more colorful indoor playground attraction with slides,

00:23:38.632 --> 00:23:39.598
games and the ball pit.

00:23:39.694 --> 00:23:43.186
Ball pits were popping up at kid friendly fast food establishments all over

00:23:43.208 --> 00:23:45.742
the country, which gave way to a lot of urban legends.

00:23:45.806 --> 00:23:48.658
Combine that with the faster spread of information during the early days of

00:23:48.664 --> 00:23:51.682
the Internet and email and these legends started to become widespread.

00:23:51.746 --> 00:23:54.022
According to About.com's Urban Legends page,

00:23:54.076 --> 00:23:57.458
It started in 1998 with rumors of a three year old receiving what appeared

00:23:57.474 --> 00:24:00.658
to be a rattlesnake bite in a Burger King ball pit in South Carolina.

00:24:00.754 --> 00:24:04.106
McDonald's would have their own version of the controversy a year later, in

00:24:04.128 --> 00:24:08.086
November 1999, when a new viral email was passed around, a woman named

00:24:08.118 --> 00:24:11.446
Lauren Archer claimed she took her three year old son Kevin to a McDonald's

00:24:11.478 --> 00:24:15.046
restaurant in Sugarland, Texas, and found a welt on him in the bath.

00:24:15.088 --> 00:24:18.478
The next day, he was vomiting, his eyes rolled back in his head, and he was taken to

00:24:18.484 --> 00:24:20.910
the emergency room, where he died later that night.

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:24.238
The autopsy revealed that Kevin had died from a heroin overdose, and the

00:24:24.244 --> 00:24:26.594
welt was caused by a needle broken off inside of him.

00:24:26.632 --> 00:24:29.858
According to the email, police emptied the ball pit to find rotten food,

00:24:29.944 --> 00:24:34.546
several hypodermic needles, knives, candy, diapers, feces, and the stench of urine.

00:24:34.568 --> 00:24:38.546
While this specific story has been debunked, there was no Kevin who

00:24:38.568 --> 00:24:41.382
died of a heroin overdose in or around Sugarland that month.

00:24:41.436 --> 00:24:44.834
It is widely believed that it comes from a place of truth, and McDonald's

00:24:44.882 --> 00:24:48.038
