00:37:38.202 --> 00:37:42.218
he retaliated by possessing statues to cause mayhem,

00:37:42.314 --> 00:37:44.474
almost as if he needed to be in the limelight.

00:37:44.522 --> 00:37:47.362
And if the company wasn't going to place him there, he would find another

00:37:47.416 --> 00:37:48.526
way to get attention.

00:37:48.638 --> 00:37:52.062
There's no way anyone could prove that the real Ronald was responsible.

00:37:52.126 --> 00:37:53.490
But the message was clear.

00:37:53.560 --> 00:37:57.346
And I think McDonald's understood that message because in 2014, they tried

00:37:57.368 --> 00:38:00.838
to make the character work one last time by giving him another makeover.

00:38:00.844 --> 00:38:02.502
In an attempt to make him less scary to kids,

00:38:02.556 --> 00:38:05.090
The jumpsuit was replaced by a vest and cargo pants.

00:38:05.170 --> 00:38:07.890
There was even a more formal sports coat for special occasions.

00:38:07.970 --> 00:38:11.090
In an attempt to further relate to this new generation of kids,

00:38:11.100 --> 00:38:12.266
Ronald got his own Instagram account.

00:38:12.368 --> 00:38:16.118
Though whether this made him less or more scary is certainly up for debate.

00:38:16.214 --> 00:38:19.434
Maybe being more spontaneous in these photos resulted in some less

00:38:19.472 --> 00:38:22.106
flattering angles that made him look even more scary.

00:38:22.218 --> 00:38:26.400
-[Chris] I wish that scary looking clown at the end of my bed would go away… AHHH!

00:38:30.450 --> 00:38:32.430
But that's just me cherry picking again.

00:38:32.500 --> 00:38:36.046
These photos mostly did no harm, but didn't really help his popularity like

00:38:36.068 --> 00:38:36.682
he expected.

00:38:36.746 --> 00:38:41.022
He reached 27,000 followers by 2016, not much compared to one of his rivals,

00:38:41.086 --> 00:38:45.174
Wendy, the mascot of Wendy's, who had 851,000 Twitter followers at that time.

00:38:45.212 --> 00:38:49.014
 But nothing, and I mean nothing, could have prepared Ronald or his

00:38:49.052 --> 00:38:51.880
company for what was about to happen next.

00:39:01.790 --> 00:39:03.020
-[Kid 1] There you are.

00:39:04.750 --> 00:39:06.140
-[Kid 1] Let go of it him!

00:39:08.350 --> 00:39:09.820
-[Kid 2] Run for it! Run!

00:39:14.110 --> 00:39:17.678
That's a clip from the movie Clown, which, after a few delays, came out in

00:39:17.684 --> 00:39:20.298
the United States on June 17, 2016.

00:39:20.394 --> 00:39:23.338
This movie mostly didn't find an audience outside of the horror movie fandom, 

00:39:23.354 --> 00:39:26.222
but it may have played a part in setting up one of the strangest

00:39:26.286 --> 00:39:29.454
and, in my opinion, best hysterias to sweep North America.

00:39:29.502 --> 00:39:36.506
That fall.

00:39:36.558 --> 00:39:38.118
-[Off camera] Come on Wesley. Come on Wesley. Wesley where are you going?

00:39:38.204 --> 00:39:40.826
-[Off camera] You’re being -- OH MY GOD! OH MY GOD! OH MY GOD!

00:39:41.210 --> 00:39:45.909
-[Off camera] OK, what the? No this is not happening.

00:39:47.909 --> 00:39:49.909
-[Off camera] This is not real.

00:39:49.915 --> 00:39:51.239
-[Off camera] HE’S RUNNING AFTER US!

00:39:51.239 --> 00:39:51.932
-[Off camera] Hit it.

00:39:51.932 --> 00:39:52.906
-[Off camera] Hit that.

00:39:52.906 --> 00:39:53.640
-[Off camera] Hit that.

00:39:55.470 --> 00:39:58.394
-[Reporter] Creepy clown sightings are happening across the country,

00:39:58.432 --> 00:39:59.274
-[Reporter] and it's no laughing matter.

00:39:59.392 --> 00:40:01.782
-[Reporter] This is an absolute nightmare.

00:40:01.926 --> 00:40:02.586
-[Off camera] Oh, my God.

00:40:02.608 --> 00:40:03.354
-[Off camera] I just want to fish dude!

00:40:03.402 --> 00:40:04.922
-[Reporter] Clown sightings.

00:40:04.986 --> 00:40:08.446
-[Reporter] The trend that's terrifying people across North America with sightings in

00:40:08.468 --> 00:40:12.330
-[Reporter] more than half of the United States, as well as Canada and Mexico.

00:40:12.490 --> 00:40:15.790
-[Reporter] Group of clowns that are trying to lure kids into the woods.

00:40:15.870 --> 00:40:17.842
-[Reporter] No one really knows why it's happening.

00:40:17.976 --> 00:40:21.470
-[Reporter] One theory is the remake of IT, based on Stephen King's book.

00:40:21.550 --> 00:40:23.886
-[Reporter] Now they're threatening school districts.

00:40:24.078 --> 00:40:25.540
-[Off camera] Dude, what the.

00:40:25.930 --> 00:40:27.000
-[Off camera] What the.

00:40:29.770 --> 00:40:31.560
-[Off camera] Hey, what are you doing?

00:40:36.410 --> 00:40:41.574
-[Reporter] Chaos on campus with hundreds of Penn State students in a state of panic.

00:40:41.702 --> 00:40:43.020
-[Off camera] Oh, my God.

00:40:44.830 --> 00:40:48.042
The McDonald's corporation was asking themselves the same thing.

00:40:48.096 --> 00:40:51.558
And with the 2016 clown craze reaching a fever pitch as Halloween approached that year,

00:40:51.574 --> 00:40:55.210
a decision had to be made about the future of Ronald McDonald.

00:40:55.290 --> 00:40:58.874
-[Reporter] He's one of the most recognizable faces to children worldwide.

00:40:58.922 --> 00:41:02.986
-[Reporter] But the recent rash of creepy clown sightings is hurting Ronald McDonald's marketability.

00:41:03.018 --> 00:41:06.594
-[Reporter] Ronald McDonald, a fixture of the McDonald's food chain since 1963 is going to take a little vacation.

00:41:06.632 --> 00:41:11.038
-[Reporter] Saying in a statement, McDonald's

00:41:11.054 --> 00:41:14.606
-[Reporter] and franchisees in the local markets are mindful of the current climate

00:41:14.638 --> 00:41:18.062
-[Reporter] around clown sightings in the communities, and as such, are being thoughtful

00:41:18.126 --> 00:41:21.958
-[Reporter] in respect to Ronald McDonald's participation in community events for the

00:41:21.964 --> 00:41:22.598
-[Reporter] time being.

00:41:22.684 --> 00:41:25.986
At this point, Ronald was the last remaining character from the old

00:41:26.018 --> 00:41:26.518
McDonaldland crew.

00:41:26.562 --> 00:41:30.374
So his being forced into a leave of absence was truly the end of an era.

00:41:30.422 --> 00:41:34.186
And after going over his entire history, watching more than 10 hours of

00:41:34.208 --> 00:41:37.926
McDonald's commercials, watching several movies and limited series,

00:41:37.958 --> 00:41:41.834
 reading hundreds of articles, and scrubbing entire social media accounts,

00:41:41.882 --> 00:41:46.270
somewhere along the way, I think I figured out Ronald's true motivation.

00:41:46.270 --> 00:41:48.816
(IMPACT)

00:41:50.965 --> 00:41:54.692
♪  Suspenseful Music ♪

00:41:55.270 --> 00:41:59.874
What is Ronald's true goal in all of this? What is the true source of his power?

00:41:59.912 --> 00:42:03.042
There are basically two constants throughout his story.

00:42:03.176 --> 00:42:04.590
Kids and magic.

00:42:04.670 --> 00:42:07.982
Throughout crafting this episode, I became convinced that they are linked.

00:42:08.046 --> 00:42:11.570
Ronald's time around kids definitely coincides with his occult activity.

00:42:11.650 --> 00:42:15.286
So I started to ask myself, what is it about kids that gives Ronald his power?

00:42:15.308 --> 00:42:19.074
At times, it appears that he may be eating them, but there's no proof

00:42:19.122 --> 00:42:21.286
and frankly, no trail of missing kids.

00:42:21.388 --> 00:42:24.682
At some point, I considered the idea that he's trying to fatten them up.

00:42:24.736 --> 00:42:28.714
But that got debunked in the 2000s when his exercise DVD still featured him

00:42:28.752 --> 00:42:29.990
using plenty of magic.

00:42:30.070 --> 00:42:33.446
The only time we really saw his magic power start to dwindle was the decade after,

00:42:33.478 --> 00:42:36.286
when he struggled to stay in touch with the youth and floundered his

00:42:36.308 --> 00:42:38.494
way through curating a failing social media account.

00:42:38.612 --> 00:42:41.950
That's when I realized his power doesn't come from kids at all.

00:42:42.020 --> 00:42:43.866
It comes from influence.

00:42:43.978 --> 00:42:46.430
Think back to that passage about Pennywise from IT.

00:42:46.500 --> 00:42:50.546
If bait were needed, why, what child did not love a clown?

00:42:50.568 --> 00:42:53.294
Pennywise took the form of a clown to lure in kids and feed on their fear.

00:42:53.342 --> 00:42:56.654
But Willard Scott turned himself into a clown because kids are the easiest

00:42:56.702 --> 00:42:57.710
people to influence.

00:42:57.790 --> 00:42:59.714
His first move was to make the kids trust him,

00:42:59.752 --> 00:43:00.882
So he gained influence.

00:43:00.946 --> 00:43:04.102
In the 80s, he convinced the kids to think he was cool by trying every

00:43:04.156 --> 00:43:06.390
activity under the sun to make himself look cool.

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:07.890
And he gained influence.

00:43:07.970 --> 00:43:11.222
He gained so much influence that he had them eating processed food,

00:43:11.276 --> 00:43:14.918
sanitized in pink slime, and climbing to epidemic levels of obesity.

00:43:15.014 --> 00:43:18.106
And when people took notice of what he was up to, he actually got those

00:43:18.128 --> 00:43:19.718
little lard balls to exercise.

00:43:19.814 --> 00:43:21.818
Look at the data from the center for Disease Control.

00:43:21.904 --> 00:43:25.790
Childhood obesity grew every year from Ronald's introduction to 2003.

00:43:25.860 --> 00:43:29.130
Right when he shifted his messaging to be all about health and clean eating.

00:43:29.210 --> 00:43:32.474
Then the numbers dipped for the first time and continued to trend downward

00:43:32.522 --> 00:43:34.622
until Ronald was sidelined in the early 10s.

00:43:34.676 --> 00:43:38.014
There were obviously other factors as well, but his 21st century exercise

00:43:38.062 --> 00:43:42.126
tirade actually worked, which means he had influence.

00:43:42.238 --> 00:43:45.618
And when he was told he had to step back from the commercials, he found a

00:43:45.624 --> 00:43:49.094
new way to influence those kids, which happens to be my favorite way to influence. 

00:43:49.132 --> 00:43:50.482
Influence by fear. 

00:43:50.546 --> 00:43:54.802
Moving statues, stories of crucified kids and ball pit mayhem.

00:43:54.866 --> 00:43:57.810
It's no wonder kids started seeing him as an icon of horror.

00:43:57.890 --> 00:44:00.662
Videos of Ronald McDonald imposters flooded the Internet.

00:44:00.726 --> 00:44:04.026
People created fan made horror games, fake commercials,

00:44:04.048 --> 00:44:06.090
3AM challenges, and bizarre viral videos.

00:44:06.240 --> 00:44:09.062
And this meant that Ronald lost control of the narrative.

00:44:09.126 --> 00:44:12.842
He no longer had the influence, they did, and Ronald's power was quickly dwindling.

00:44:12.896 --> 00:44:15.838
His Instagram went quiet in 2021.

00:44:15.924 --> 00:44:19.258
Today, Ronald still makes occasional appearances from time to time, popping

00:44:19.274 --> 00:44:21.946
up on McDonald's social media or surfacing at a parade.

00:44:21.978 --> 00:44:25.006
But for the most part, his time in the limelight seems to be over.

00:44:25.108 --> 00:44:28.946
Even his old frenemy Grimace got a bigger marketing push in 2023 than he did.

00:44:28.968 --> 00:44:32.994
It seems that in the world of influencers and social media, Ronald can

00:44:33.032 --> 00:44:36.038
get the attention of kids, but he can't keep it like he once could.

00:44:36.124 --> 00:44:40.006
His cult of children was no more, and that's why I found it interesting when I came across this. 

00:44:40.028 --> 00:44:48.182
-[Nissim] The cross his his symbol, and he use them to make his point. 

00:44:48.236 --> 00:44:49.634
-[Nissim] We are slaves.

00:44:49.682 --> 00:44:55.158
-[Nissim] We have new God instead, of the old God, and we pray for McDonald's.

00:44:55.254 --> 00:44:56.422
This is McJesus.

00:44:56.486 --> 00:44:59.606
Not to be confused with the Edmonton Oilers’ center, a life size sculpture

00:44:59.638 --> 00:45:03.166
created by Finnish artist Jani Leinonen, which went up in Haifa, Israel in 2019.

00:45:03.188 --> 00:45:07.834
After 56 years, it seems Ronald finally found someone more easily

00:45:07.882 --> 00:45:11.274
influenced than children, super religious people.

00:45:11.322 --> 00:45:14.458
According to independence, the piece sparked protests which turned violent and

00:45:14.474 --> 00:45:17.634
three police officers were injured as demonstrators tried to break into where the statue was being held.

00:45:17.672 --> 00:45:19.614
People were deeply offended.

00:45:19.662 --> 00:45:22.782
The culture minister threatened to cut funding, and the sculpture ultimately

00:45:22.846 --> 00:45:24.450
had to be removed for the time being.

00:45:24.520 --> 00:45:28.386
But this was probably still a win for Ronald because the chaos that he

00:45:28.408 --> 00:45:30.210
created was still influence.

00:45:30.290 --> 00:45:33.526
The statue hasn't emerged again since then, but don't be surprised if it

00:45:33.548 --> 00:45:36.806
somehow disappears from wherever it's being stored or turns its head and

00:45:36.828 --> 00:45:38.082
speaks to the night watchmen.

00:45:38.146 --> 00:45:41.702
The only question is how far McDonald's will go to cover it up.

00:45:41.756 --> 00:45:45.046
Like Pennywise, Ronald is dormant again... for now.

